From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MementoRC <MementoRC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove --export-all-symbols from libclang-cpp on MinGW

When building with zig cc, the MinGW dllcrt2.obj defines atexit.
--export-all-symbols forces all symbols (including atexit) to be
exported regardless of dllexport annotations. Removing it lets
MinGW lld's default auto-export behavior handle symbol export.

The atexit collision with libLLVM's import library is handled
separately in build.sh by stripping the symbol post-build.

---
 clang/tools/clang-shlib/CMakeLists.txt | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/clang/tools/clang-shlib/CMakeLists.txt b/clang/tools/clang-shlib/CMakeLists.txt
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/clang/tools/clang-shlib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/clang/tools/clang-shlib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -60,10 +60,3 @@ if (NOT APPLE AND NOT MINGW AND NOT LLVM_LINKER_IS_SOLARISLD_ILLUMOS)
   target_link_options(clang-cpp PRIVATE LINKER:-Bsymbolic-functions)
 endif()
-if (MINGW OR CYGWIN)
-  # The clang-cpp DLL is supposed to export all symbols (except for ones
-  # that are explicitly hidden). Normally, this is what happens anyway, but
-  # if there are symbols that are marked explicitly as dllexport, we'd only
-  # export them and nothing else. Therefore, add --export-all-symbols to
-  # make sure we export all symbols despite potential dllexports.
-  target_link_options(clang-cpp PRIVATE LINKER:--export-all-symbols)
-endif()
